// Chapter: Deployment. Arc is environment -> dependencies -> serving -> eval
// -> freeze, with dungeon/smiles as the one running example.
// Written 2026-10-03 from source: mim v0.33.0 (morloc-manager working tree),
// morloc-nexus (mcp.rs, cli.rs), compiler HEAD. Transcripts marked as such
// were run by the author; the rest of the commands await a verification run,
// and their output is described in prose rather than shown.

The entry point to the Morloc ecosystem is `mim` (Morloc Installation
manager). This tool was introduced in the <<installing>> section. Now we will
show its end-to-end use in managing and deploying Morloc environments.

This chapter walks the full deployment path with one program. The program is
`smiles`, a small chemistry library that wraps the Python
https://www.rdkit.org[RDKit] package. By the end you will have built an
environment for it, installed it, served its functions over MCP and a JSON API,
let callers compose new expressions from it, and frozen the result into an
image.

